PATCH 218: reconstruct FUN_0000_8f9f (a DCBS per-type object INIT method dispatched by c296's tail
near-vector, object-type 2) -- the same DGROUP-near-offset base-loss class as 7b91/8744/973a (patches
215/216/217).  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x8f9f.

Reached as the DCBS roster-install cascade advances (43c1 -> c296 -> per-type dispatch
word[DGROUP:(word[di]*2-0x1b20)]).  Ghidra base-lost di (param_1 treated as a HOST pointer -> SIGSEGV);
DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, every [di+N] is a DS-relative byte/word field.  Reconstructed with the explicit
g_mem+0x1c000 base + the asm byte/word widths (the 1e27 tail copies a seg template into DGROUP:di+off,
a near-offset dst which 1e27 bases internally, patch 087).  Validated by the crash advancing strictly
forward (COOP_TICK, deterministic).

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (reached ONLY via the FIST_CASCADE FSG DCBS
parse).  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.
